      "body": "Deployment verified on 2026-09-18 at 18:45:24 UTC. Both healthy Fly Machines and public `/version` report approved commit `ab9bbacc9da845b6bfe70ac3fda2ace44f17c918`, immutable image `sha256:6d233d65e5c9121e25277e96b51e0415c550cf280ec89e8c5deed098a32bf6a9`. This tested mail-only ancestor is now contained in main; it preserves the prior production base and avoids the unfinished parallel identity release. Build Image 35372584021 passed all jobs. The protected release completed without rollback; the prior compatible image and a fresh volume snapshot are retained.\n\nA real production password-reset request to the explicitly authorized owner Gmail was received in INBOX/CATEGORY_PERSONAL with aligned SPF/DKIM/DMARC PASS, and the application's Date/Message-ID covered by DKIM. Including the earlier SMTP/template tests, four received messages reached Principal. This does not prove universal inbox placement or a spam-to-inbox reputation improvement. No password was changed and no recovery link was opened.\n\nThe reviewed exclusion secret is Deployed. DMARC `rua` now agrees across all three authoritative servers and Google/Cloudflare resolvers. The daily read-only monitor's 18:50 UTC run succeeded: 13 DSNs in its 14-day window, zero aggregate DMARC reports, no read errors. Original spam samples and authorized Outlook/enterprise destination accounts remain unavailable.\n\nProduction verification also found that successful SMTP events can remain buffered on stdout. Follow-up #458 changes those two writes to stderr, matching the error event; it has its own review and checks. No claim that this final logging adjustment is deployed yet.\n",
